+# Local MAPF Online Integration Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Integrate the bounded four-agent LocalConflictResolver into active Fleet Adapter GoToPlace planning as an opt-in PoC and validate it with failure-injected unit tests and Docker/MQTT simulation.
+
+**Architecture:** A fleet-owned coordinator serializes ownership on the fleet worker, asynchronously confirms physical quiescence, preserves stationary schedule occupancy, solves on a separate worker, and performs schedule-first non-atomic group application with explicit recovery. Legacy planning and negotiation remain the fallback.
+
+**Tech Stack:** C++17, RMF Traffic/Fleet Adapter, RxCpp workers, Catch2, ROS 2, Docker Compose, Python MQTT/simulator instrumentation.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-03-local-mapf-online-integration-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Feature default is off; no VDA5050 command gate, external arbiter, corridor state machine, or real robot deployment.
+- Preserve `rmf_traffic` baseline `ccdb765`, LocalConflictResolver commit `e569de3`, and all existing user files/worktrees.
+- Maximum local group size is the code-level hard limit of four; runtime configuration may only lower it.
+- Never report fallback as a safety or deadlock-resolution guarantee.
+- Holding/bay arrival is not task completion; every accepted plan retains the original active task goal.
+- Do not call group application atomic; test schedule and execution failure stages independently.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Telemetry that repeats an identical pose with a fresh timestamp must establish freshness without creating a false movement revision; Task 1 tests it.
+- Stop acknowledgement without a fresh stationary report must time out without local application; Task 1 tests it.
+- A result whose plan start is in the past must re-snapshot/re-solve rather than time-shift; Task 3 tests it.
+- Negotiation arriving during partial execution start must own cleanup before issuing its command; Task 4 tests it.
+- Recovery after any partial failure must publish stationary occupancy before legacy replan; Tasks 2 and 4 test it.
+
+---
